   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.4. Increased capacity of Member States to improve social dialogue and labour relations laws, processes and institutions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">A manual for training the chairpersons, Facilitators, and workplace forum members was developed in March 2022, and the capacities of all members of the Work Place Forums (WPF) have been strengthened through training conducted from May 2022.
All four WPFs at the Pilot sites adopted constitutions for operating the WPFs in May 2022 and conducted regular meetings. The fifth WPF was established in September 2023.
19 Ministry Secretaries endorsed the rollout of the Dispute Resolution Mechanism across the entire Public Sector in September 2022. The ILO developed a manual for training the chairpersons, facilitators, and members of the pilot Workplace Forums. The officials of the Ministry of Public Administration were capacitated to support the rolling out of the Public Sector Dispute Resolution Mechanism to other priority sectors. The ILO supported the establishment of a special Unit &quot;Workplace Cooperation Unit&quot; at the Ministry that would act as the operation Hub for the rollout and implementation of the mechanism.</narrative>
   </description>
