  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.4. Increased capacity of Member States to improve social dialogue and labour relations laws, processes and institutions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dispute resolution prevention mechanisms were established in 2023 within pilot sectors in the public sector (i.e., public transport and public health). 
The Ministry of Labour and Foreign Employment (MoLFE) established a tripartite Task Force to support the development of a joint response to the country&apos;s economic crisis and its impact on the labour market and industrial peace.
Employers&#x2019; organizations introduced grievance handling guidelines at the enterprise level in selected sectors (i.e., service sectors, banking, finance and manufacturing) 
Ministry of Public Administration submits a cabinet paper requesting approval to set up Sectoral Councils

 ILO provided technical assistance to promote the principles of social dialogue, and workplace cooperation, including facilitating a high-level consultation for 19 Ministry secretaries to secure their buy-in for the rollout of the dispute resolution mechanism.
The ILO designed and implemented a manual for training for the chairpersons, Facilitators, and workplace forum members.  
The ILO, through RBSA-funded initiatives, capacitated the employers&apos; organizations on grievance handling and workplace cooperation guidelines.</narrative>
   </description>
